=== Key insight check ===
WKB spin 9 at t=4: terms = [((0, 0), 0)]
Certified spin 9 at t=4 (first 5): [((10, 0), 1), ((8, 2), 15), ((8, 0), -5), ((6, 4), 120), ((6, 2), -95)]

The WKB gives ONLY the PI^2 term (PX^0), while certified has full polynomial.
This means the WKB 'charge' at the exceptional point is NOT the full charge,
but only the subleading (in PX) component. The monic normalisation then fails
because it expects the leading PX^(s-1) term which has vanished.
